  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The mode table (`MACHINE_MODES`), its captions, the menu row text, the door tip phrase and `set_machine_mode` moved out of `actions.rs` into `crates/ui/src/machine_modes.rs`. `actions.rs` is 400 lines (main: 433).\n- The table has a fourth row: `Plasma cutting`, mounting the built-in `Tormach 1300PL` through the same undoable `LoadBuiltinMachine`.\n- The door (the narrow ribbon cell) wears the plain caption only.\n- The door tip lists the modes from the table (no hand-typed list).\n- The menu rows add the sections a mode adds to a mill, read from the registry, only when the caption does not already name them.\n- The menu is as wide as its longest row (measured with the row font), never narrower than the usual 200 px.\n- `machine_rows` takes the width; its doc comment no longer says \"three\".\n\n## What a user sees\n\nDoor (ribbon cell): `Milling…`, `Turning…`, `Mill-turning…`, `Plasma cutting…` (the plain caption of the mounted mode).\n\nDoor tip: \"Switch the workspace: Milling, Turning, Mill-turning or Plasma cutting (mounts the kind's built-in machine, undoable)\".\n\nMode menu rows:\n- Milling\n- Turning\n- Mill-turning - Turning\n- Plasma cutting\n\nThe current row reads \"<row> (current)\". The menu is widened to fit that text.\n\n## Choices (decision file `docs/decisions/1195-plasma-machine-mode.md`)\n\n- The explicit table is kept (not derived from `posting::MACHINES`). `machine_mode_tests::every_kind_with_a_shipped_machine_has_a_mode` and `every_mode_mounts_a_shipped_machine_of_its_own_kind` pin it. No EDM row, since no EDM machine ships.\n- Menu rows name only the sections a mode adds beyond a mill, from the registry (`shown_for`, `Section::label`). A mill-turn also keeps every mill section; its row says only what it adds.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::machine_mode_tests` (new file, 7 tests): every shipped kind has a mode; every mode mounts its own-kind shipped machine; menu row text; the door wears the plain caption for every mode; the door tip lists every mode; the menu width; Milling -> Plasma cutting -> Milling with the plasma section shown, Plasma Profile creatable, a repeated pick mounting nothing, and two undos restoring the mill.\n- `egui_app::tests::the_machine_door_switches_workspaces_and_rides_undo` (row count 4) and the door tip pin in `tests.rs` (new text).\n\n## Gates (final head `fe37c1ae`, after merging origin/main)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 593 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not seen on screen. The menu width and the door's fit are unverified visually.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Snapshot PNGs are not touched. The ribbon's pixel goldens (`crates/ui/tests/snapshots/`) will differ at the next cut.\n\nChangelog: ribbon machine modes gain Plasma cutting (mounts the Tormach 1300PL); the menu names the sections a mode adds (#1195, PR)\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1195\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
